hadiths[38]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16606","Waki narrated to us, he said: Abu Umays narrated to us, from Iyas ibn Salamah, from his father, he said: I dueled a man and killed him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me his spoils."
"16607","He said: Waki narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa, from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man eating with his left hand and said: Eat with your right hand. He said: I cannot. He said: May you not be able. He said: And it did not return to him."
"16608","He said: Waki narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Iyas ibn Salamah, from his father, he said: I killed a man, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who killed this man. They said: Ibn al-Akwa. He said to him: His spoils are his."
"16609","He said: Waki narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Iyas ibn Salamah, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a boy named Rabah."
"16610","He said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Yala ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: I heard Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa, from his father, he said: We used to pray Friday with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then return and find no shade of the walls in which to seek shade."
"16611","He said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Iyas ibn Salamah, from his father, he said: We raided Hawazin by night with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had put him in command over us."
"16612","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa, from his father, he said: Our watchword on the night we raided Hawazin by night with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had put him in command over us, was: Die, die. And I killed with my hands on that night seven people of houses."
"16613","He said: Bahz narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar al-Yamami narrated to us, he said: Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa narrated to us that his father narrated to him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to a man called Busr ibn Rai al-Ir, whom he saw eating with his left hand: Eat with your right hand. He said: I cannot. He said: May you not be able. He said: And his right hand did not reach his mouth after that. And Abu al-Nadr said in his hadith: Ibn Rai al-Ir from Ashja."
"16614","He said: Bahz narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Iyas ibn Salamah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever draws the sword against us is not from us."
"16615","He said: Bahz narrated to us, from Ikrimah ibn Ammar, he said: Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man sneezed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on you. Then he sneezed again, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The man has a cold."
"16616","Bahz narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, Iyas ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: We went out with Abu Bakr ibn Abi Quhafah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had put him in command over us. He said: We raided Fazarah, and when we drew near the water, Abu Bakr ordered us and we rested late at night. He said: When we prayed the dawn prayer, Abu Bakr ordered us and we launched the raid. We killed at the water those we killed. Salamah said: Then I looked at a group of people with offspring and women heading toward the mountain, and I was running after them, and I feared they would beat me to the mountain, so I shot an arrow and it fell between them and the mountain. He said: I brought them driving them to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, until I came to him at the water, and among them was a woman from Fazarah wearing a cloak of leather, and with her a daughter of hers from the finest of the Arabs. He said: Abu Bakr gave me her daughter as extra spoils. He said: I did not uncover her garment until I arrived at Madinah, then I spent the night and did not uncover her garment. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me in the market and said to me: O Salamah, give me the woman. I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah she pleased me, and I have not uncovered her garment. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent and left me, until on the next day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me in the market and said: O Salamah, give me the woman, may your father be bereft of you. I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah she pleased me, I have not uncovered her garment, and she is yours, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent her to the people of Makkah, and in their hands were captives from the Muslims, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ransomed them with that woman."
"16617","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ibn Shihab: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Kab ibn Malik al-Ansari informed me that Salamah ibn al-Akwa said: On the day of Khaybar, my brother fought fiercely with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then his sword recoiled upon him and killed him. The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke about that and doubted concerning him, a man who died by his weapon; they doubted something of his affair. Salamah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from Khaybar, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you permit me to chant rajaz for you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted him. Umar said to him: Know what you say. He said: I said: By Allah, were it not for Allah we would not have been guided, nor given charity, nor prayed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You spoke the truth. So send down tranquility upon us, and make firm the feet when we meet, and the polytheists have transgressed against us. When I finished my rajaz, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who said this. I said: My brother said it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah some people fear to pray over him, saying: A man who died by his weapon. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He died striving, struggling. Ibn Shihab said: Then I asked Ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa, and he narrated to me from his father like what Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, except that Ibn Salamah said: He also said with that, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They fear to pray over him; they lied. He died striving, struggling, so he has his reward twice. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured with his two fingers."
"16618","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, from Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali, from Jabir ibn Abdullah and Salamah ibn al-Akwa, a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that they both said: We were in an expedition, and the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: Enjoy yourselves."
"16619","He said: Qurran ibn Tammam narrated to us, from Ikrimah al-Yamami, from Iyas ibn Salamah, from his father, he said: I went out with Abu Bakr in the expedition of Hawazin, and he gave me a slave girl as extra spoils, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked her from me as a gift, and sent her to Makkah, and ransomed with her some people from the Muslims."
"16620","He said: al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd narrated to us, from Salamah ibn al-Akwa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"16621","He said: Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn Abi Ubayd, from Salamah ibn al-Akwa that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a man from Aslam to announce among the people on the day of Ashura: Whoever was fasting, let him complete his fast, and whoever had eaten, let him not eat anything, and let him complete his fast."
"16622","He said: Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd, from Salamah that he sought permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the desert life, and he permitted him."
"16623","He said: Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd, from Salamah ibn al-Akwa, he said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the people at al-Hudaybiyah, then sat aside, and when the people dispersed from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O Ibn al-Akwa, will you not pledge allegiance. I said: I have pledged, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Again. I said: Upon what did you pledge. He said: Upon death."
"16624","He said: Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn Abi Ubayd, from Salamah, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a bier was brought. He said: Did he leave any debt. They said: No. He said: Did he leave anything. They said: No. He said: Then he prayed over him. Then another was brought, and he said: Did he leave any debt. They said: No. He said: Did he leave anything. They said: Yes, three dinars. He said: Then he said with his finger: Three brands. He said: Then the third was brought, and he said: Did he leave any debt. They said: Yes. He said: Did he leave anything. They said: No. He said: Pray over your companion. A man from the Ansar said: His debt is upon me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then he prayed over him."
"16625","Hammad narrated to us, from Yazid, from Salamah, he said: Amir was a poet, and he dismounted chanting, saying: O Allah, were it not for You we would not have been guided, nor given charity, nor prayed. So forgive as ransom for You what we have done, and make firm the feet when we meet, and cast tranquility upon us. When we are called we come, and to the callers they rely upon us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is this driver. They said: Ibn al-Akwa. He said: May Allah have mercy on him. A man said: It is binding, O Messenger of Allah, why did you not let us enjoy him. He said: He was struck; he went to strike a Jewish man, and the edge of the sword hit the eye of his knee. The people said: His deed was void; he killed himself. He said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after he arrived at Madinah, while he was in the mosque, and said: O Messenger of Allah, they claim Amir's deed was void. He said: And who says it. I said: Men from the Ansar, among them so-and-so and so-and-so. He said: He who said it lied. He has two rewards, with his two fingers, and he is striving, struggling, and few Arabs walked upon it seeking you against him."
"16626","He said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Yazid, meaning Ibn Abi Ubayd, informed us, from Salamah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his crier on the day of Ashura that whoever had eaten in the morning, let him abstain, and whoever had not eaten in the morning, let him complete his fast."
"16627","Safwan said, from Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd, from Salamah, he said: When we arrived at Khaybar, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw fires being kindled and said: Upon what are these fires kindled. They said: Over the meat of domestic donkeys. He said: Break the pots and pour out what is in them. He said: A man from the people stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we pour out what is in them and wash them. He said: Or that."
"16628","He said: Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd narrated to us, from Salamah ibn al-Akwa, that he informed him, he said: I went out from Madinah heading toward al-Ghabah until when I was at Thaniyyat al-Ghabah, a boy belonging to Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf met me. He said: I said: Woe to you, what is the matter with you. He said: The milch camels of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were taken. He said: I said: Who took them. He said: Ghatfan and Fazarah. He said: I shouted three shouts, making all between its two lava tracts hear: O morning attack, O morning attack. Then I rushed until I met them while they had taken them. He said: I began shooting at them and saying: I am Ibn al-Akwa, and today is the day of al-Aqra. He said: I rescued them from them before they drank. I came driving them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the people are thirsty, and I hastened against them before they drank, so go after them. He said: O Ibn al-Akwa, you have gained power, so be lenient. The people are being entertained among their people."
"16629","Makki narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd narrated to us, he said: I saw the trace of a blow on the leg of Salamah and said: O Abu Muslim, what is this blow. He said: This is a blow I received on the day of Khaybar. He said: On the day I was struck, the people said: Salamah is wounded. I was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he blew into it three blows, and I have not complained of it until now."
"16630","Ibrahim ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Hatim, meaning Ibn Ismail, narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd, he said: I heard Salamah ibn al-Akwa saying: I went out, and he mentioned similar to the hadith of Makki, except that he said: And today is the day of al-Rudda. And he added in it: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounted me behind him on his mount."
"16631","He said: Makki narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd narrated to us, he said: I used to come with Salamah to the mosque, and he would pray at the pillar that is near the mushaf. I said: O Abu Muslim, I see you seek prayer at this pillar. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking prayer at it."
"16632","He said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Rashid al-Yamami narrated to us, he said: Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa narrated to us, from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Aslam, may Allah grant them peace, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive them. Indeed, by Allah, I did not say it, but Allah said it."
"16633","He said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah narrated to us, he said: Iyas narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: We arrived with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Hudaybiyah, and we were fourteen hundred, and over it were fifty sheep that would not water it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat at its edge, and either he supplicated or spat, and it gushed, and we drank and drew water. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for the pledge at the root of the tree, and I pledged to him first of the people, and he pledged and pledged until when he was in the midst of the people he said: O Salamah, pledge to me. He said: I have pledged to you first of the people, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And also, so pledge. He saw me unarmed and gave me a hajafah or daraqah, then he pledged and pledged until when he was among the last of the people he said: Will you not pledge to me. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have pledged first of the people and middlemost of them and last of them. He said: And also, so pledge. I pledged to him. Then he said: Where is your daraqah or hajafah that I gave you. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my uncle Amir met me unarmed, so I gave it to him. He said: He said: You are like the one who said: O Allah, grant me a beloved who is more beloved to me than myself. And he laughed. Then the polytheists corresponded with us for peace until some of us walked to others. He said: I was a servant of Talhah ibn Ubaydullah; I groomed his horse and watered him and ate from his food, and I had left my family and wealth emigrating to Allah and His Messenger. When we made peace, we and the people of Makkah, and some of us mingled with others, I came to the tree, swept its thorns, and lay in its shade. Four men from the people of Makkah came to me and began, while they were polytheists, disparaging the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I moved from them to another tree, and they hung their weapons and lay down. While they were thus, a caller called from the bottom of the valley: O company of the Muhajirun, Ibn Zunaym was killed. I drew my sword and rushed upon the four and took their weapons and made them a bundle. Then I said: By the One who honored Muhammad, no man among you shall lift his head except I strike that in which are his eyes. I came driving them to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and my uncle Amir came with Ibn Mikraz, leading his horse, leading seventy, until we halted them. He looked at them and said: Leave them; they shall have the beginning of wickedness. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pardoned them, and there was revealed: And He it is who withheld their hands from you and your hands from them. Then we returned to Madinah, and we stopped at a stopping place called Lahy Jamal. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought forgiveness for whoever climbed the mountain that night, having been a scout for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions. I climbed that night twice or thrice. Then we arrived at Madinah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent his camels with his boy Rabah, and I was with him. I went out with a horse of Talhah to graze it with the camels. In the morning, Abd al-Rahman ibn Uyaynah al-Fazari raided the camels of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), drove them all away, and killed its herdsman."
"16634","He said: Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa narrated to us, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at a stopping place, and a spy for the polytheists came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions were eating the morning meal. They invited him to their food, and when the man finished, he mounted his mount and went swiftly to warn his companions. Salamah said: I caught him, made his mount kneel, and struck his neck. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me his spoils."
"16635","He said: Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ibrahim, from Salamah ibn al-Akwa, he said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I am sometimes in hunting, and I pray in my shirt. He said: Button it, even if you find only a thorn."
"16636","He said: Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Utbah, from Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer and the supper are present, begin with the supper."
"16637","He said: Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Attaf narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi Rabiah, he said: I heard Salamah ibn al-Akwa, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am in hunting, and I pray with nothing on me but one shirt. He said: Button it, even if you find only a thorn."
"16638","Hashim ibn al-Qasim said, he said: Ikrimah narrated to us, he said: Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Hawazin. He said: While we were taking the forenoon meal, most of us on foot with weak ones among us, a man came on a red camel. He pulled a rope from behind his saddle and hobbled his camel with it, a young man. Then he came eating lunch with the people. When he saw their weakness and the meagerness of their mounts, he went out to his camel, freed it, then made it kneel and sat upon it, and went out galloping. A man from Aslam from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) followed him on a gray she-camel that was the best mount of the people. He pursued him. He said: I went out running and caught him, the head of the she-camel at the haunch of the camel, and I was at the haunch of the she-camel. Then I advanced until I was at the haunch of the camel, then I advanced until I seized the bridle of the camel and made it kneel. When it placed its knee on the ground, I drew my sword and struck his head with it, and it fell off. I came with his mount and what was upon it, leading it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me coming forward. He said: Who killed the man. They said: Ibn al-Akwa. He said: All his spoils are his."
"16639","He said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd, he said: Salamah ibn al-Akwa narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None shall say falsehood about me, or what I did not say, except he shall take his seat in the Fire."
"16640","He said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd, he said: Salamah ibn al-Akwa narrated to us, he said: We went out to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Khaybar, and a man from the people said: O Amir, let us hear from your tunes. He said: He dismounted driving them and mentioning: By Allah, were it not for Allah we would not have been guided. And he mentioned poetry other than this, but I did not memorize. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is this driver. They said: Amir ibn al-Akwa. He said: May Allah have mercy on him. A man from the people said: O Prophet of Allah, why have you not let us enjoy him. When the ranks faced each other, they fought them, and Amir ibn al-Akwa was struck by the hilt of his own sword and died. In the evening they kindled abundant fire, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is this fire, upon what is it kindled. They said: Over domestic donkeys. He said: Pour out what is in them and break them. A man said: Shall we not pour out what is in them and wash them. He said: Or that."
"16641","He said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd, he said: Salamah ibn al-Akwa narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man from Aslam: Announce among your people, or among the people, on the day of Ashura: Whoever ate, let him fast the rest of his day, and whoever had not eaten, let him fast."
"16642","He said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Yazid, he said: Salamah ibn al-Akwa narrated to us, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a bier was brought. They said: O Prophet of Allah, pray over it. He said: Did he leave anything. They said: No. He said: Did he leave any debt upon him. They said: No. He prayed over him. Then another bier was brought after that, and he said: Did he leave any debt upon him. They said: No. He said: Did he leave anything. They said: Three dinars. He said: Three brands. He said: The third was brought, and he said: Did he leave any debt upon him. They said: Yes. He said: Did he leave anything. They said: No. He said: Pray over your companion. A man from the Ansar called Abu Qatadah said: O Messenger of Allah, his debt is upon me. He prayed over him."
"16643","He said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd, he said: Salamah ibn al-Akwa narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to a people from Aslam while they were shooting in the market and said: Shoot, O Banu Ismail, for your father was an archer. Shoot, and I am with Banu so-and-so, for one of the two parties. They held their hands. He said: Shoot. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how shall we shoot while you are with Banu so-and-so. He said: Shoot, and I am with all of you."
